      "reasoning": "All seven current fields are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-38540: x=-5(1,-2), so [x]_B=(0,-5); multiplying by [T]_{B|C} gives (0,-10,-10). q-126031: integrating (1+x)^(-2) from 2 to infinity gives 1/3. q-343302: Abel's identity gives W'=-W/(x^2+1), hence W=C exp(-arctan(x)); W(0)=2 gives C=2, so W never vanishes on the real line. q-86676: using the eigenvectors as columns of P gives G=P diag(-1,2) P^(-1)=[[-16,9],[-30,17]]; direct multiplication verifies both prescribed eigenpairs. q-81190: the eigenvalues are 3i and -3i, and the eigenvector component ratios are 5/(1+3i) and 5/(1-3i). Their product is 25/10=5/2, unchanged by independent eigenvector scaling. The four previously reviewed questions retain their earlier field answers. The earlier batch's source errors belong to questions absent from this current contract and do not affect this judgment. No submitted grade is provided; MA evidence here comes exclusively from the captured worked solutions.",
